o. 11 South Carolina</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/mens-soccer-mountaineers-draw-with-no-11-south-carolina</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/mens-soccer-mountaineers-draw-with-no-11-south-carolina</guid><category>Men's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Isaac Scheer battles for the ball against South Carolina" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/3/MSOCvsUofSC-45.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – In a top-20 matchup at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium, the No. 16 West Virginia University men's soccer team and No. 11 South Carolina played to a 1-1 draw, Saturday night. The Mountaineers go to 5-1-3 this season and 1-0-2 in the Sun Belt while the Gamecocks are now 7-1-2 and 1-0-2 as well in conference play.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/MSOCvsUofSC-45.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/MSOCvsUofSC-45.jpg"><media:title>Isaac Scheer battles for the ball against South Carolina</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/MSOCvsUofSC-45.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:47:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>6</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59482</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Beat Penn State for First Time Since 2010, Drop Meet to Virginia Tech</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/mens-swimming-diving-mountaineers-beat-penn-state-for-first-time-since-2010-drop-meet-to-virginia-tech</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/10/3/mens-swimming-diving-mountaineers-beat-penn-state-for-first-time-since-2010-drop-meet-to-virginia-tech</guid><category>Men's Swimming &amp; Diving</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Two WVU men's swimmers flex their muscles while at practice." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/10/3/GB701627.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University men's swimming and diving team picked up a win against Penn State for the first time since 2010 and lost to No. 11 Virginia Tech at the Christiansburg Aquatic Center in Christiansburg, Virginia, on Saturday.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/GB701627.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/GB701627.jpg"><media:title>Two WVU men's swimmers flex their muscles while at practice.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/10/3/GB701627.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:26:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>7</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59481</s:story_id></item></channel></rss>